From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:23:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 107/342] kernel debug level 2 again: level 1 panics at boot on
 arm64

With KDEBUG_LEVEL 1 the ODROID-C2 panicked during the boot's device
registration (fdt, meson_i2c, the I2C bus, devfs publish_device): a
synchronous exception whose iframe could not be pushed, a write to a
read-only page of main2's kernel stack, 4.6 KB into a 16 KB stack. Not
understood yet. The fixes the level 1 build needed (a signal frame read
compiled out with ASSERT, the FDT bus manager's calls in ASSERTs, three
build failures) stay: they are right at any level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h b/build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h
index a3c598b9e5..404cb94e48 100644
--- a/build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h
+++ b/build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 // 0: Disables all debug code that hasn't been enabled otherwise.
 // 1: Enables some lightweight debug code.
 // 2: Enables more debug code. Will impact performance.
-#define KDEBUG_LEVEL 1
+#define KDEBUG_LEVEL 2
 
 #define KDEBUG_LEVEL_2	(KDEBUG_LEVEL >= 2)
 #define KDEBUG_LEVEL_1	(KDEBUG_LEVEL >= 1)
